## COMPUTATIONAL IMPLEMENTATION

### QuTiP Framework

```python
from qutip import *

# 1. System definition
I = qeye(2)
sm = destroy(2)
n = sm.dag() * sm

# 2. Tensor operators for 3 qubits
n0 = tensor(n, I, I)
n1 = tensor(I, n, I)  
nz = tensor(I, I, n)

# 3. Hamiltonian
H = 2.0*n0 + 1.5*n1 + 0.5*nz + 0.005*(|101⟩⟨010| + h.c.)

# 4. Lindbladian
c_ops = thermal_bath(sm0, e0, beta0, gamma0) + \
        thermal_bath(sm1, e1, beta1, gamma1) + \
        thermal_bath(smz, ez, betaz, gammaz)

# 5. Solve steady-state
rho_ss = steadystate(H, c_ops)

# 6. Extract metrics
Jz = Tr(H * dissipator(smz, rho_ss))
```

### Scaling via Tensor Train

For larger systems (N > 3 qubits):

```
GKSL: Memory = O(2^(2N)), Operations = O(2^(3N))
TT:   Memory = O(N·D⁴), Operations = O(N·D³)

At N=8:
  GKSL needs 256 MB, TT needs <1 MB
  Speedup: ~500×
```

